# Company Import Workflow

Use for **create** candidates not already in Oracle. Pattern mirrors `det_import_uploader.py`.

## Template

- **Authoritative source:** `C:\Users\<USERNAME>\Downloads\COMPANY_IMPORT_SAMPLE (7).xlsx`
- Preserve native Excel structure exactly (styles, `q` sheet, validations, OOXML metadata). Do **not** rebuild via openpyxl/pandas DataFrame — that strips formatting and Edit Tool may reject or mis-parse the file (Format Painter from sample `(7)` is the recovery path if format drifts).
- Prefer `native-create-template` / `build_native_create_template.py` cloning rows from sample `(7)`.
- Copy template, fill row 2+, clear sample values only; keep formatted blank cells.

## Populate only these fields

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| COMPANY_NAME | Exact legal name |
| ADDRESS | Street or PO Box line |
| CITY / STATE / ZIP | From SOS/source |
| ADDRESS_TYPE | `S` street, `P` PO Box, `U` if unclear |
| BUSINESS_TYPE | `L` LLC, `I` inc, `C` corp, `U` if unclear |
| LOCATION_TYPE | `1` for HQ/legal entity |

**Do not populate `ESTABLISH_DATE`** (or other optional sample columns) unless <OPERATOR> explicitly asks.

## Upload

- Script: `scripts/edit_tool_company_import_uploader.py`
- Page: `http://<EDIT_TOOL_HOST>/web/EditToolLive/Company/Import`
- POST fields: `ImportFile` (xlsx), `Email` (required)
- Auth: Chrome CDP cookies (`EDIT_TOOL_CDP_URL`, default `http://127.0.0.1:9222`)
- Grid poll: `/web/EditToolLive/Company/ImportedCompaniesGrid`
- Success UI text: **Import started. You will receive an email upon completion.**

```powershell
python scripts\edit_tool_company_import_uploader.py C:\path\company_import.xlsx --submit --match "COMPANY NAME" --poll-oracle
```

## After SAFE returns

- Write SAFE back to review workbook.
- Group-structure adds use `SET_COMPANY_RELATION` / move SQL only after <OPERATOR> approves.
